infra/provision.sh	AWS CLI provisioning path for the required EC2 hosts after Terraform was unavailable.
infra/bootstrap.sh	Idempotent EC2 host bootstrap and environment capture script.
infra/README_RUN.md	Provision/destroy runbook and cost notes.
tools/clock_probe.cpp	Independent UDP ping-pong clock residual probe source; not run because provisioning failed.
benchmark/run_remote.sh	Remote EC2 benchmark orchestrator with receiver bind polling and result pullback.
reports/ec2_pass/00_manifest.log	Manifest of files produced in this pass.
reports/ec2_pass/01_provision.log	Quota, identity, Terraform check, and failed run-instances output.
reports/ec2_pass/02_bootstrap.log	NOT_RUN bootstrap reason.
reports/ec2_pass/03_clock.log	NOT_RUN clock methodology reason and rejected local alternative.
reports/ec2_pass/04_instrumentation.log	Instrumentation changes and NOT_RUN verification reason.
reports/ec2_pass/05_baseline.log	NOT_RUN baseline A/B reason.
reports/ec2_pass/06_rate_sweep.log	NOT_RUN rate sweep reason.
reports/ec2_pass/07_fec_verdict.log	NOT_RUN FEC verdict reason.
reports/ec2_pass/08_fanout.log	NOT_RUN fan-out reason and 16 vCPU fallback note.
reports/ec2_pass/09_batch_tuning.log	NOT_RUN batch tuning reason.
reports/ec2_pass/10_teardown.log	Exact cleanup commands and five required empty verification queries.
reports/ec2_pass/11_final_report.md	Synthesis, blockers, open items, spend, and teardown confirmation.
reports/ec2_pass/env/NOT_RUN/provision_failed.txt	Placeholder env evidence explaining why no host env dump exists.
reports/ec2_pass/comment_grep.txt	Empty literal comment marker grep output for modified/authored code files.
reports/ec2_pass/acceptance_checks.log	Git, syntax, and no-comment acceptance evidence.
reports/ec2_pass/acceptance_commands.sh	Bash command wrapper used to capture numeric acceptance exit codes.
reports/ec2_pass/teardown_commands.sh	Narrow exact-resource teardown command wrapper.
reports/ec2_pass/file_sizes.txt	Local non-empty file-size verification for report files.
reports/ec2_pass/verify_nonempty.sh	Bash helper used to verify required logs are non-empty.
